  "description": "Chip Authentication after BAC, id-CA-ECDH-3DES-CBC-CBC over Brainpool P-256. DG14 carries one ChipAuthenticationInfo (version 1, no keyId) and one id-PK-ECDH ChipAuthenticationPublicKeyInfo (named-curve SPKI). The DESede suite is a single MSE:Set KAT (00 22 41 A6) whose data is DO91(uncompressed ephemeral point); DO84 is absent because DG14 carried no keyId (the keyId-0 asymmetry is vector-pinned instead). Secure messaging then restarts under 3DES with SSC = 8x00, and the final step is the first post-CA protected command (SELECT eMRTD AID): it proves the derived keys, as the post-PACE SELECT does. Chip responses are port-synthesised from the simulated PICC (chip private scalar 2a1cd7b4..., terminal ephemeral 3f8e0d5b...). runners omitted = both.",
